    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ălytarcha</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-es</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλυτάρχης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a magistrate who
				superintended religious exhibitions</i>, Cod. Th. 10, 1,
			12.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ălytarchĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the office of such
